<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson 9 mo profit rises 30 percent.</title>
<headline>Ericsson 9 mo profit rises 30 percent.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>LM Ericsson AB reports for nine months to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Sales					78,201 vs  66,901</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			    6,258 vs   4,810</p>
<p> New orders (rises 22 pct)	    95,628 vs     n/a</p>
<p> EPS (skr)				    4.47 vs    3.60</p>
<p> Other operating income		  1,064 vs     416</p>
<p> Interests in associates		   581 vs     326</p>
<p> Costs of goods sold		    42,898 vs  36,343</p>
<p> Costs of sales, R&amp;D, admin	   27,616 vs  23,568</p>
<p> Depreciation				2,992 vs   2,616</p>
<p> Financial income			  1,119 vs     950</p>
<p> Financial costs			     927 vs     922</p>
<p> Profit after financial items	  6,532 vs   5,144</p>
<p> Minority interests		 CHARGE 274 vs     334 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax charge				  1,907 vs   1,493</p>
<p> Net profit				  4,351 vs   3,317</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full company name is LM Ericsson AB. Analysts polled by Reuters expected a nine-month pre-tax profit of 6.24 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
